# Branch dispute reviewer & Kontrol-only payment — OPS-OQ-1a / OPS-OQ-1b (rule 204)

Extends rule 203; where they differ, this rule wins **only** for §D.18 (who
reviews) and §C.13 (whether a Kontrol invoice may be paid alone). Everything else
in rule 203 stands unchanged.

Evidence: `docs/sprints/hardening-rme-billing-dispute-branch-reviewer-control-payment-1.md`.
Architecture: `docs/architecture/rme-billing-dispute-escalation.md` §OPS-OQ-1a/1b.
Operator guidance (Bahasa Indonesia): `docs/operations/rme-billing-dispute-sop.md`.

## A. The owner decisions

01. **OPS-OQ-1a — approved.** An explicitly designated branch responsible person
    may review and resolve branch-scoped billing disputes with legitimate
    resolution evidence. Provenance: the owner's instruction in the brief of this
    sprint. No signed artefact exists and none is fabricated.
02. **OPS-OQ-1b — approved.** A legitimate Kontrol invoice may be paid on its own
    while its originating visit invoice is under an active billing dispute; the
    payment is allocated to the Kontrol invoice only and the origin stays exactly
    as it was. Same provenance.
03. **The all-branch dispute policy (OPS-OQ-1, rule 203) is unchanged.** A known
    wrong amount is still not collected; a disputed invoice is still held on every
    payment path; the patient is still never held.

## B. Who reviews (OPS-OQ-1a)

04. **Explicit designation, never a role.** Authority comes from one row in
    `mst_rme_billing_dispute_reviewers` naming ONE account and ONE branch,
    created by an account holding `manage_rme_billing_dispute_reviewers`. That
    permission is granted to **no operational role** — Super Admin holds it
    through the existing `'*'` grant.
05. **Branch-scoped.** A designation authorizes review, note, escalate and resolve
    on disputes of **that branch only**, and only while the account's
    server-resolved working scope (`RmeWorkingBranchScope`) reaches that branch.
    Both are required; neither substitutes for the other.
06. **No role inheritance.** Front Office is the exact union of Admin Klinik and
    Kasir; a role grant would reach all eight Front Office accounts. Designations
    are per account and never inherited, so they cannot leak through a role.
07. **No Front Office review — implicit or explicit.** Holding
    `manage_rme_billing` (report / note) never implies review, and a counter
    account (`Front Office`, `Kasir`) can never be designated
    (`BILLING_DISPUTE_REVIEWER_COUNTER_ROLE`, brief §13). The counter reports; a
    designee reviews. Admin Klinik and Supervisor RME accounts may be designated
    explicitly — they hold billing rights, which is why §15 adds independence.
08. **Super Admin keeps its existing authority** through `'*'` and is unaffected
    by designations.
09. **Owner stays read-only.** An Owner account cannot be designated
    (`BILLING_DISPUTE_REVIEWER_OWNER_READ_ONLY`); `view_rme_billing_disputes`
    remains its only dispute permission.
09a. **Eligibility is revalidated on every use**, not only at the grant
    (`RmeBillingDisputeReviewerService::isEligibleDesignee()` — one rule for the
    grant, the policy, the service and the routing): an account that later
    becomes Owner, Front Office or Kasir, or loses RME workspace access, keeps
    its row but loses its effect at once. Revoke the row afterwards for clarity.
10. **Active account only.** The designee must be a usable account (active, not
    soft-deleted) with RME workspace access (`view_clinic_visits` or
    `manage_clinic_visits`) at designation time, and it is re-read from the
    database on every action — a deactivated designee is refused
    (`ACTOR_UNUSABLE`) even with a live session.
11. **Revocation** sets `revoked_at` / `revoked_by` / `revoke_reason` (all three,
    enforced by a database CHECK); revoked rows are immutable and never deleted;
    the very next action of that account on that branch is refused.
12. **Branch transfer invalidates in practice.** The designation names the branch,
    not the person: a context-bound account (Admin Klinik, Kasir, Perawat, Front
    Office) transferred to another branch keeps an active row but loses the
    working scope, so its next action is refused (`BRANCH_OUT_OF_SCOPE`). An
    account that is not context-bound keeps a scope over every RME branch, so for
    it the designation row itself is the only branch limit. Revoke the row when
    the person no longer holds the branch responsibility.
13. **Reviewer audit.** `RME_BILLING_DISPUTE_REVIEWER_DESIGNATED`, `…_REVOKED` and
    `…_REFUSED` (every refusal — authorization AND eligibility — with its stable
    `[CODE]`) carry ids, codes and the reason length only — never the free text,
    a patient name, NIK/KTP or clinical content.
14. **Resolution evidence is unchanged.** A designee resolves exactly as a
    permission holder does: `CORRECTION_APPLIED` (server-verified) or
    `ORIGINAL_CONFIRMED_CORRECT` (reference recorded, invoice unchanged). No
    override, waiver or "close without evidence" exists.
15. **No self-certification.** The reporter may not confirm the original
    (`SELF_RESOLUTION_FORBIDDEN`); a DESIGNEE who issued the invoice
    (`cashier_id`), recorded a payment on it, or requested / decided / applied a
    correction of it may not confirm the original either
    (`RESOLVER_NOT_INDEPENDENT` — "independent confirmation", brief §14;
    Super Admin's rule-203 path is unchanged); the governor may not designate itself
    (`SELF_DESIGNATION_FORBIDDEN`, plus a database CHECK `user_id <> granted_by`);
    a holder of the review permission is refused as redundant. A designation
    carries **no** invoice price edit, correction maker/checker, refund, debt
    forgiveness, cancellation, manual PAID or guard override.

## C. The Kontrol-only payment (OPS-OQ-1b)

16. **B may be paid alone** — `RmePaymentService::payControlInvoiceOnly()`, reached
    only by the explicit `payment_scope=control_only` + `confirm_control_only`
    form; the service itself also requires `confirm_control_only`, so a future
    non-HTTP caller states the intent too. It is never inferred; without it the
    ordinary rules apply unchanged.
17. **Eligibility:** every OUTSTANDING origin of the Kontrol chain (payable, same
    branch, remaining > 0) has an ACTIVE dispute. No outstanding origin →
    `CONTROL_ONLY_PAYMENT_NOT_APPLICABLE`. Any outstanding origin NOT disputed →
    `CONTROL_ONLY_PAYMENT_ORIGIN_NOT_DISPUTED` (fail closed on a mixed chain:
    collectable debt is collected by the ordinary rule, never skipped).
18. **Allocation to B only.** Exactly one payment row, on B. The request carries no
    origin id and no allocation; forged ones are ignored — the service re-derives
    the chain under the locks.
19. **Rp0 to A.** No payment row is ever written for the origin on this path.
20. **Origin receivable preserved:** A's grand total, remaining and payment history
    are unchanged; it stays UNPAID/PARTIAL and in the receivable report.
21. **Origin status preserved:** A's status, version and dispute are unchanged; the
    dispute stays active until legitimately resolved.
22. **No carry-over debt forgiveness.** The Kontrol visit completing on its own
    settlement does not waive, reallocate or rewrite A's balance.
23. **Multi-invoice atomicity.** The ordinary combined payment (`allocateControlPayment`)
    and any visit batch that would settle a disputed origin are still refused
    whole (`BILLING_DISPUTE_ACTIVE`) — rule 203 §C.13 holds for them.
24. **D10 compatibility.** An active correction on B holds the B-only payment
    (`assertNoPaymentHold`); a dispute on B holds it too.
25. **D28 compatibility.** Nothing here changes the Rp0-original correction guard.
26. **Invoice version safety (rule 191).** B is settled only at the version the
    form carries (`PATH_CONTROL_ONLY`); A's version is neither required nor
    changed. An origin correction applying concurrently is unaffected.
27. **Cross-branch Kontrol (OD-1)** stays allowed; the B-only path applies to B's
    own branch only.
28. **Receivable isolation (OD-1a):** another branch's origin is neither shown nor
    collected here; the eligibility rule considers same-branch origins only.

## D. Preserved controls

29. **Maker / checker** of corrections is unchanged (maker 29, checker 1, D1e).
30. **SPN4 pilot restrictions** stand: corrections stay SPN4-only (D1c). The B-only
    payment is all-branch, like the dispute policy, and needs no correction.
31. **Payment actor authority.** The cashier is the persisted, usable account with
    `manage_rme_billing` whose working branch is B's branch — re-read under the
    invoice lock (rules 197/198).

## E. Concurrency, verification, operations

32. **PostgreSQL locking contract.** Dispute action: invoice → dispute → designation
    (`FOR SHARE`); revocation takes only the designation (`FOR UPDATE`). B-only
    payment: B → each origin (`FOR UPDATE`) — the ordinary control path's own
    order, so no new lock edge exists. Races A–N run on PostgreSQL 16
    (`RmeBillingDisputeBranchReviewerConcurrencyTest`) and skip, stated, on SQLite.
33. **Mutation tests** target designation required, branch match, revocation,
    inactive actor, self-grant, origin dispute required, B-only allocation, A
    untouched, D10, B dispute, version check and combined-payment denial.
34. **Independent security review** precedes merge; no unreviewed CRITICAL/HIGH.
35. **Financial reconciliation:** the B-only payment writes
    `RME_PAYMENT_CONTROL_ONLY_ORIGIN_DISPUTED` with the held origin and dispute ids
    and `allocated_to_origin = 0`; receipts and reports show B's payment only.
36. **Rollback protection.** Rolling back to the rule-203 runtime is fail-closed
    for both decisions: it still honours every dispute hold, ignores designations
    (only Super Admin reviews again) and offers no B-only path (the combined
    payment is refused whole again). B-only payments already recorded are ordinary
    payment rows and stay historically accurate. Never roll back BELOW rule 203
    while `rme:billing-dispute-status` reports an active dispute; never delete
    designation or dispute rows; never run the migration's `down()` on a database
    that holds designations; never rewrite a payment.
37. **VPS-only deployment** — `scripts/deploy-vps-runner.sh` runs inside the VPS;
    completion is `DEPLOY_EXIT_CODE=0`, `DEPLOY_STATUS=DEPLOY_OK`,
    `DEPLOY_HEAD_TARGET_MATCH=YES`.
38. **Production verification is read-only:** no designation, invoice, dispute or
    payment is created to prove behaviour; production starts with zero designations.
39. **GO tag** names the exact deployed runtime SHA and scopes only this hardening;
    it is never a full prepayment-pilot GO.
40. **Cleanup** removes only task-owned resources by exact path.
